    "narrative": "Heading into August 24th, our offensive strategy centers on exploiting matchups against weaker arms while leaning into our high-speed assets. The clear priority today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads our squad with a 75.69 score. While he faces a respectable arm in Gausman, the combination of a favorable batting order spot, park factors, and a massive +4% bump for targeting a slow pitcher delivery makes him an elite play. We also see a significant platoon advantage for **Seiya Suzuki** (71.14), whose projection is elevated by a massive +19% boost thanks to the generous 5.27 xERA of Kelly. Additionally, **Henry Bolte** (61.01) is a mandatory start; his placement at the top of the order combined with the high-score potential against Matthews makes him a high-floor producer in a category where we desperately need to chase stolen bases.\n\nWe have maintained a disciplined bench today, enforcing our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" to preserve our game caps for more opportunistic windows. **Zach McKinstry** came the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his 38.26 score fell just short due to the difficult matchup against Rasmussen and a negative platoon split. Similarly, **Cole Young** was considered against Wheeler, but his 33.13 rating was suppressed by Wheeler\u2019s elite stuff and the defensive efficiency of the opposing catcher, keeping him on the pine. We are monitoring **James Wood** on the IL, hoping for his return to bolster our depth, while **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined by a team off-day. \n\nWe must navigate today\u2019s slate with caution regarding **Josh Naylor** (48.34) and **Gabriel Moreno** (56.63), both of whom are facing difficult matchups against Wheeler and Gausman, respectively. **Naylor** is particularly at risk today, as the combination of a premier starter and unfavorable park factors significantly handicaps his base projection. While we are starting him, he remains on the low end of our confidence interval. We have avoided the trap of starting players like **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, or **Travis Bazzana** today, as their current configurations do not meet the minimum efficiency threshold required to burn a game cap against today's defensive alignments.",
